* text=auto eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.ini text eol=lf
*.properties text eol=lf
# Archives are binary; never translate line endings inside them.
*.tar.gz binary
*.tgz binary

# Recorded reports, compared byte for byte by tests/test_baseline.py.
#
# The CSVs carry CRLF row terminators because that is what the csv module
# writes and what the published files therefore contain. `* text=auto eol=lf`
# above would normalise them to LF on checkout, and the comparison would fail
# on a fresh clone and in CI while passing on the machine that recorded them.
# `-text` disables every conversion, so these arrive exactly as committed.
tests/fixtures/expected/** -text
